      "title": "Gas temperature falls quickly up the riser",
      "description": "Hot gas (~ 150–600 °C depending on product) picks up the wet particles at the venturi and carries them up the duct at high velocity (~ 10–30 m/s). Surface moisture flashes off within seconds, so the gas temperature falls rapidly; the short contact time makes flash dryers suitable for heat-sensitive, free-flowing materials with mainly surface moisture.",
